# QSM Guest Agent

This package is installed **inside a Linux VM**, not on Proxmox.

1. Enable QSM Display1 in VM Hardware -> Display and restart the VM. This
   creates `org.qsm.direct.agent` on virtio-serial.
2. Install the package in the guest: `sudo apt install ./qsm-guest-agent_*.deb`.
3. Select the logged-in desktop user once. This enables the per-user system
   agent; if the VM was not restarted after step 1 it will start automatically
   when the virtio port next appears:
   `sudo qsm-guest-agent-setup USER`.
4. Log in again. For a Wayland desktop, enable its bridge once:
   `systemctl --user enable --now qsm-guest-clipboard.service`.

The agent uses `~/.local/share/qsm-guest-agent/incoming` for browser uploads
and `~/.local/share/qsm-guest-agent/outgoing` for files that the browser may
download. In the QSM Direct Console, drag a local file onto the guest picture
to place it in `incoming`; place a guest file in `outgoing`, open **Files**,
then download it or drag its prepared browser item where the browser supports
host drag-out. The browser cannot write arbitrary local paths without user
consent, so **Download** remains the portable guest-to-client action.

The agent transfers only plain UTF-8 clipboard text (up to 1 MiB) and files
with a plain basename (up to 2 MiB). It lists only these two exchange folders;
it never exposes the guest home directory. `wl-clipboard` is required for the
Wayland clipboard bridge; install it with `sudo apt install wl-clipboard`.
